nodes.body:
Thanks @Begunner, you're right. `switch_to_trainer()` sleeps hybrid replicas without a weight update, so my "only at a weight update" claim was wrong for that path, and a shared Mooncake store would lose entries standalone replicas still use. I've updated the docs.

@aoshen02 vllm#57810 looks like the right fix for that path: under `salt`, verl would pass `clear_connector_cache=False` on sleep/release. I'll wire it in once it lands, in this PR or a follow-up, whichever you prefer.

To be clear about scope: #57810 keeps a store when the weights don't change. This PR is for when they do. The salt invalidates old-weight entries without wiping the store, which is what stores without a working reset (LMCacheMP, HF3FS, SGLang HiCache storage) and stores shared across replicas or jobs need.

